    {
        "content": "<p>To avoid getting myself into a big XY problem, I find it rather inelegant that programs written with <code>IO</code> (or even <code>ST</code>) cannot have properties proven about it, and I don't have complete control over <code>Task</code>. Currently I want to be able to write something like \"when no task can proceed, resolve this promise\", but I can't think of how to check for \"when no task can proceed\" without a centralized event loop…</p>\n<p>(but either way, I find the above problem independently interesting, and if someone already made such a thing, I figure I'd better know about it)</p>",
        "id": 634619317,
        "sender_full_name": "user202729",
        "timestamp": 1792845655
    }
]